{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: let gs artifact and gs review-request republish or refile at the same head when the intent changed.\n\nWhy. gs artifact derives each act's idempotency key from (actor, head, path), and gs review-request from (actor, head). On 2026-09-17 a same-head republish with a changed intent was refused four times with \"idempotency key reused with different intent: \u003ckey\u003e already names an accepted act this filing does not rebuild\": twice when a reviewer asked that documentation artifacts rest on the implementation artifact they describe (a provenance correction the source head does not change), and twice when the corrected set needed a fresh review request at the same head. Each time the work went through gs batch with hand-written keys, three or four acts, and a hand-written supersede of the predecessor, which is exactly the shape the step commands exist to remove. The keys are right for the retry they protect (the same publication filed twice appends nothing) and wrong for the case they refuse (the same path at the same head with different bases or text is a new publication that succeeds its predecessor).\n\nOutcome. gs artifact at a head where the signer already has a live artifact at that path treats a changed intent as a republish: it files the new artifact under a key that includes what changed, retires the predecessor with the new artifact as its successor in the same batch, and says so; an unchanged intent still replays. gs review-request at a head where the signer already has a live request refuses as today unless --replace, and --replace files the new request under a key that includes the artifact set it rests on, retiring the old one; an unchanged set still replays. Both commands print the predecessor they retired, and neither needs gs batch for a provenance correction.","body":{"branch":"request/same-head-republish","conditions":"1. gs artifact at a head where the signer holds a live artifact at a named path with different --rests-on or --text files a successor and retires the predecessor in the same batch, printing the retirement; the same invocation repeated appends nothing. 2. gs review-request --replace at a head where the signer holds a live review request files the replacement and retires the old one even when the head is unchanged, when the artifact set or text differs; an identical invocation replays. 3. Tests pin: same-head republish with added bases succeeds with one live artifact per path afterwards; identical retry appends nothing; same-head --replace refile succeeds; the refusal message on a key conflict, where one remains, names the repair. 4. docs/reference/gs/artifact.md and review-request.md describe the same-head republish and refile. 5. go test ./... green at the exact head; independent review by codex; ratified; landed on main and pushed.","target_head":"ccd161c6caa71f800bfdf17796d11bb3419f181f","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}